{"event_type":"review","id":"d44d49147ebfbd2a7a48438b3711fa8803140ed3a21e9eb85de567843cb2949e","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T00:29:37Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/140ed45f7df3ef54c8dc9be66e625f2b8495802945141527163661ff48afb29a","sha256":"140ed45f7df3ef54c8dc9be66e625f2b8495802945141527163661ff48afb29a"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/e10cd2cfed8f968ee9f542844f080000e1a6faca3b21a51c8b9bbdecd7d32b09","sha256":"e10cd2cfed8f968ee9f542844f080000e1a6faca3b21a51c8b9bbdecd7d32b09"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/25af3d9b18eb2c92c3d3f5e4668a42dd4dee743711ffbb07357251c29bc22f66","sha256":"25af3d9b18eb2c92c3d3f5e4668a42dd4dee743711ffbb07357251c29bc22f66"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/ef174f73761a6b4dd5835fe4cf618be7dec9d4e59e0d05be98bee770d3d13663","sha256":"ef174f73761a6b4dd5835fe4cf618be7dec9d4e59e0d05be98bee770d3d13663"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6807abfd54aaf34102f23f953998679683a9fcdfb5b240d9cc6f3442a9956aee","sha256":"6807abfd54aaf34102f23f953998679683a9fcdfb5b240d9cc6f3442a9956aee"}],"attempt_id":"522465552c571fe0f5fff650f4049ea438dc91fa287c752b95bc3637d1b59812:0:1","base":"9bcbd24b9db947378864680f2039e89c2f7c2db0","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"d8f8f2d62f4c46a5c0d63dad05221b2d9a98a13f","body":"**Remove the conflicting repair-role instructions.**\n\n`apps/crq-python/README.md:96-98` says dispatch uses GLM only. The policy at `apps/crq-python/README.md:154-156` still assigns Luna, Muse, and Sol to repair roles. Update the older paragraph so operators have one dispatch contract.","id":"5e182d59befeec3d21886948b0c805c199e82b029b11efcb965e46a8bb90c552","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/README.md","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Remove the conflicting repair-role instructions."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"c8834fa5df0b9ee5930ff1cb4e120442a5c11ab2","body":"**Catch `AttributeError` in the receipt loop.**\n\nSeveral `.get` calls in the `try` block run on values read from the receipt document. The `except` clause catches only `KeyError`, `TypeError`, `ValueError`, and `OSError`, so an `AttributeError` from these calls escapes the loop.\n\n- `status_summary.py:72`: `capture.get(\"equivalence\")` runs before `current_equivalence` checks the type of `capture`. If `capture` is not a dict and equals `origin.get(\"capture\")` on line 71 (for example, both are `None`), the call raises `AttributeError`.\n- `status_summary.py:80-82` and `status_summary.py:91`: `p.get` and `path.get` run on each element of `capture[\"paths\"]`. `current_equivalence` checks only that `paths` is a list, not that each element is a dict. Line 91 runs for every terminal category that passes classification.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        except (KeyError, TypeError, ValueError, OSError):\n+        except (KeyError, TypeError, ValueError, AttributeError, OSError):\n             counts[\"unverified\"] += 1\n```\n\n</details>","id":"8731cfc7ada586ad9fa6ca1e8eaa01eab8263fbded78b9cddbea17f09f2c8491","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/status_summary.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Catch `AttributeError` in the receipt loop."}],"head":"c0f199ebf77941045e27566dbb0e64314309d7f5","head_tree":"74119e2e60617e97b4070712a18195b8b48c1179","input_scope":[{"blob":"d8f8f2d62f4c46a5c0d63dad05221b2d9a98a13f","intervals":[[5,12],[18,58],[61,62],[64,105],[109,110],[132,148],[167,168],[179,179],[183,183],[210,213]],"path":"apps/crq-python/README.md"},{"blob":"c8834fa5df0b9ee5930ff1cb4e120442a5c11ab2","intervals":[[4,4],[32,108],[110,115],[129,132],[134,134],[138,139],[221,221],[236,236],[239,239]],"path":"apps/crq-python/status_summary.py"},{"blob":"154286df44c00e8531b4a274103f649c276541b5","intervals":[[153,153],[167,167],[214,233],[241,242],[470,471],[508,508],[518,533],[583,584],[629,637],[705,707],[709,712],[715,715],[719,719],[734,797],[892,893],[895,896],[980,1084]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_author_quota.py"},{"blob":"4ab03a128f05c34b8293dbfadc4d7219b3bd9f19","intervals":[[19,26],[28,31],[33,61],[76,76],[128,206]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_status_summary.py"}],"job_id":"522465552c571fe0f5fff650f4049ea438dc91fa287c752b95bc3637d1b59812:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"d1f8bcb6ca908b9c95668f3f9eef2fb3a7a43efc","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/README.md"},"merge":"8966f1b196a5be24d9ab09f4a4d760c3bfb5b745","method":"pre-merge","pre":"8fc58c222a6ef018e64427a4509c38f5d96ec8e4","source_path":"apps/crq-python/README.md"},"blob":"d8f8f2d62f4c46a5c0d63dad05221b2d9a98a13f","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/README.md","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"c11f82531d631b4d1af73950753825c70fb2b62d","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/status_summary.py"},"merge":"8966f1b196a5be24d9ab09f4a4d760c3bfb5b745","method":"pre-merge","pre":"8fc58c222a6ef018e64427a4509c38f5d96ec8e4","source_path":"apps/crq-python/status_summary.py"},"blob":"c8834fa5df0b9ee5930ff1cb4e120442a5c11ab2","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/status_summary.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"f562954891ff7945de0606dcc9cdaf288a27732d","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/test_author_quota.py"},"merge":"8966f1b196a5be24d9ab09f4a4d760c3bfb5b745","method":"pre-merge","pre":"8fc58c222a6ef018e64427a4509c38f5d96ec8e4","source_path":"apps/crq-python/test_author_quota.py"},"blob":"154286df44c00e8531b4a274103f649c276541b5","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/test_author_quota.py","reason":"boun